Chapter: ProbeCharOps

 The char operations the Char = CCE-code migration flips, measured on both
 arms before and after (agreed, Steve + Claude, 2026-08-19: the zig plug
 converges on the C#/bare-metal identity model). probe-char-literal covers
 literals and char-at; this covers the rest of the family.

 On bare metal char-code and code-to-char are identity and classification
 is BANDED: letters are 13..64 and 97..127 with punctuation 65..96 between,
 digits are 3..12. The zig plug's codepoint Char happens to agree wherever
 the tier-0 table is bijective (all of 0..127), so the identity round-trip
 and the digit band agree everywhere and the divergence is exactly the
 SECOND letter band: accented and Cyrillic codes classify as letters on
 bare metal and as non-letters through zig's a-z/A-Z test. After the
 migration every line must match bare metal.

 Expected on bare metal:

   rt15 15
   letter-a 1
   letter-punct 0
   letter-accent 1
   letter-cyrillic 1
   digit-0 1
   digit-e 0
   c2t-len 1
   c2t-byte 15

 The zig arm before the migration prints letter-accent 0 and
 letter-cyrillic 0 and matches everywhere else.

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("rt15 " & show (char-code (code-to-char 15)))
    print-line-uni ("letter-a " & show (if is-letter (code-to-char 15) then 1 else 0))
    print-line-uni ("letter-punct " & show (if is-letter (code-to-char 70) then 1 else 0))
    print-line-uni ("letter-accent " & show (if is-letter (code-to-char 100) then 1 else 0))
    print-line-uni ("letter-cyrillic " & show (if is-letter (code-to-char 115) then 1 else 0))
    print-line-uni ("digit-0 " & show (if is-digit (code-to-char 3) then 1 else 0))
    print-line-uni ("digit-e " & show (if is-digit (code-to-char 13) then 1 else 0))
    print-line-uni ("c2t-len " & show (text-length (char-to-text (code-to-char 15))))
    print-line-uni ("c2t-byte " & show (char-code-at (char-to-text (code-to-char 15)) 0))
  end
